---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { SITE_NAME } from '../lib/site.mjs'
import { pageEntities } from '../lib/entities.mjs'

const total = pageEntities.length
const tier1 = pageEntities.filter((entity) => entity.sourceTier === 'TIER_1_OFFICIAL').length
const description = `How ${SITE_NAME} checks every Grand Theft Auto VI fact before publishing it, what the four source levels mean, and how to tell us when something is wrong.`
---
<BaseLayout title="About and sources" description={description} path="/about">
  <h1>About this site</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    Grand Theft Auto VI has not been released. Almost everything written about it
    online is a guess repeated until it sounds like a fact. This site exists to
    keep the two apart.
  </p>

  <h2>The one rule</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing is published here without a source you can click. Every entry names
    where the fact came from and the date it was checked. If no reliable source
    says a thing, the thing is not on the site, even when every other site has it.
  </p>

  <h2>The four source levels</h2>
  <p>Every page carries one of these labels, in plain words, at the top.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Official source.</strong> Rockstar Games, Take-Two, the PlayStation
      Store, or the Xbox Store said it themselves. This is the strongest level.
      {tier1} of the {total} entries on this site sit here.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Major press.</strong> A large publication with a named reporter
      published it. Strong, but not the publisher's own word.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Community source.</strong> Players or fan researchers spotted it in
      a trailer or a screenshot. Useful, and clearly marked as weaker.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No source.</strong> Nothing reaches the site at this level. It is
      listed only so you know the scale is complete.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What this site will not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Publish a leak, a rumour, or a datamine as though it were a fact.</li>
    <li>Guess a release date, a price, a file size, or a map size.</li>
    <li>Pretend to have played a game that nobody has played.</li>
    <li>Fill an empty field with a number copied from an older GTA game.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When something is wrong</h2>
  <p>
    Rockstar announces things often, and a page that was right in the morning can
    be wrong by evening. Every page shows the date its source was last checked.
    If you find something out of date or plainly wrong, the
    <a href="/contact">contact page</a> is the fastest way to tell us, and
    corrections go up the same day.
  </p>

  <h2>Who runs it</h2>
  <p>
    This is an independent site run by one person. It is not affiliated with
    Rockstar Games or Take-Two Interactive, and it speaks for neither. All
    trademarks belong to their owners.
  </p>

  <h2>How it pays for itself</h2>
  <p>
    The site shows adverts and may earn a commission on some shopping links. That
    never changes what is written. A fact does not get upgraded because a link
    next to it pays.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
